From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:15:52 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - cross-region world data for relaxed thread
 checks (LightingLuminol)

Port of LightingLuminol's ReferenceCountedRegionizedWorldDataPool (GPL-3.0, Bacteriawa, revision 72d51c4d) and the worldDataPool call sites of its minecraft patch 0001 "Base Dirty Patches", as dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.compat.luminol.RegionizedWorldDataPool / WorldDataAccess leases: ServerLevel.sourbycraft$worldDataPool() hands any thread the RegionizedWorldData of the region that owns a chunk, holding a ticket while the lease is open, so an off-thread entity add/remove, tracker, spawn-chunk, block-event, neighbour update, scheduled tick, capture, redstone-time, explosion-cache or populate access reaches the structure that region ticks instead of the caller's region or null. Gated on guards/ThreadChecks.RELAXED_SCOPE (static final): an enforced server keeps the base's getCurrentWorldData() paths. The hottest capture-flag reads (Level.getBlockState and friends) only tolerate a missing region instead of going through the pool; the explosion density cache locks its two touch points. Owner decision 2026-10-22 "Tiru penuh LightingLuminol"; the ticket prevents an unload, not a merge or split, and a relaxed server is unsafe and unqualified.

